      "settings": {
        "heading": "Are Outdated Water Pollution Rules Putting Your Family’s Health At Risk?",
        "content": "<p>Water quality standards are regulated by the Environmental Protection Agency (EPA), which sets limits on safe levels of germs and chemicals in our water supply.<br/><br/>However, many water experts say these limits are dangerously outdated. <br/>A coalition of 13 green groups is currently suing the EPA, arguing they have breached federal law and failed to update these safe limits in line with new standards.<br/><br/>Under federal law, the EPA needs to update limits on pollution every five years. Yet the pollution control standards in the lawsuit haven’t been updated for an average of 34 years!<br/><br/>Experts say this lack of change has allowed dirty industries to pollute rivers and bays for years and put the health of American families at serious risk.</p>",
        "video_id": "",
        "features_heading": "",
