        "heading": "Infants And Children Among Millions Of Americans At Risk Of Hidden Mystery Illnesses",
        "content": "<p>Water contamination affects much more than just the taste or smell of your water. Scientists at the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) found more than 7 million cases of 17 different waterborne illnesses occur each year – including bacterial, parasitic, and viral infections.<br/><br/>Infants, young children, pregnant women, older adults and people with weakened immune systems are considered more likely to get sick.<br/><br/>Unfortunately, because these contaminants are impossible to see, people may fall ill without realizing their drinking water is the cause. This can mean you face a series of doctors’ appointments and tests trying to uncover the mystery illness.</p>",
